Year = {2010},
Pages = {96-100},
Note = {Conference on Modern Research in Psychology: Quantitative vs Qualitative
   Research, Sibiu, ROMANIA, MAY 21-23, 2010},
Abstract = {The purpose of the present study was to analyze the impact of emotional
   state on each dimension of organizational citizenship behavior.
   Specifically, the aim was to emphasize the relationship between the
   emotional state and the level of organizational citizenship behavior
   displayed, supported by a statistical significant correlation. Secondly,
   the study deals with the convergent validity of the two OCB
   questionnaires specifically pointing out those dimensions of OCB
   considered to be measuring the same behavior. Results based on a 55
   employees sample indicate a modest correlation between the general and
   recent emotional state and global OCB score, civic virtue and helping
   scale. As to the convergent validity, correlation between helping and
   altruism r=.279 (p=.039) is to be discussed. The helping scale also
   correlates with four other dimensions of OCB, therefore an incongruence
   of the constructs might come into discussion. Together with the
   limitation, the implications of the results, both theoretical and
   practical, are discussed as a starting point for further studies in this
   direction.},
