   (ICEESE 2017)},
Series = {IOP Conference Series-Earth and Environmental Science},
Year = {2018},
Volume = {128},
Note = {3rd International Conference on Energy Equipment Science and Engineering
   (ICEESE), Beijing, PEOPLES R CHINA, DEC 28-31, 2017},
Organization = {Wuhan Univ; Guizhou Minzu Univ},
Abstract = {Water body could affect the thermal environment and airflow field in the
   building districts, because of its special thermal characteristics,
   evaporation and flat surface. The thermal influence of water body in
   Tongji University Jiading Campus front area was evaluated. First, a
   suitable evaporation model was selected and then was applied to
   calculate the boundary conditions of the water surface in the Fluent
   software. Next, the computational fluid dynamics (CFD) simulations were
   conducted on the models both with and without water, following the CFD
   practices guidelines. Finally, the outputs of the two simulations were
   compared with each other. Results showed that the effect of evaporative
   cooling from water surface strongly depends on the wind direction and
   temperature decrease was about 2 similar to 5 degrees C. The relative
   humidity within the enclosing area was affected by both the building
   arrangement and surrounding water. An increase of about 0.1 similar to
   0.2m/s of wind speed induced by the water evaporation was observed in
   the open space.},
