   21-26, 1998},
Organization = {Int Assoc Water Quality},
Abstract = {This study aims to simulate pollutant runoff into Lake Biwa using the
   Macro Model and examine the runoff characteristics of pollutants from
   urban nonpoint sources. As a result of the simulations of all rivers
   flowing into Lake Biwa, the characteristics of urban nonpoint source
   pollution and the basic units of urban nonpoint pollutants in the Lake
   Biwa basin became clear. It was shown that the control of pollutant
   runoff from nonpoint sources during storm events was significant in
   order to protect the water quality of Lake Biwa. From these results,
   valuable data concerning the environmental management of the Lake Biwa
   basin was obtained. (C) 1998 IAWQ Published by Elsevier Science Ltd. All
