Title = {Research on computer aided concept design based perception with sketch},
Booktitle = {INTERNATIONAL VIEW LOCAL DESIGN MULTI-DISCIPLINE FUSION-CAID \& CD' 2007},
Year = {2007},
Pages = {22-26},
Note = {8th International Conference on Computer-Aided Industrial Design and
   Comceptual Design, Seoul, SOUTH KOREA, AUG 22-24, 2007},
Abstract = {In the phase of concept design, the designer usually catches the design
   inspiration and originality with informal sketches, but the current CAD
   systems need precise input, unsuitable for sketch. We cry for a CAD tool
   to support the concept design, and capture the designer's instantaneous
   afflatus and creation, to eliminate the gap between concept design and
   detail engineering design. Based the simulation of the mankind's
   perception thinking, this paper presented an algorithm for 3D model
   reconstruction from isometric drawing, a kind of sketch usually used by
   designers. The hidden information was gained through analyzing vertexes
   of hidden edges, reasoning the direction and the length of connected
   edges and the edges going through connected vertexes. Thus, some
   possible vertexes were got. After further validation with. superposition
   and the edge circuits, the correct hidden element's coordinates
   information and those circuits information. Furthermore, through
   analyzing the process and mechanism of the projection of isometric
   drawing, we developed a method to seek the lost depth information. With
   the recovering of hidden information and depth information, the model
   according to the isometric drawing was rebuilt and the sketch of the
   designer's creation realized quickly. A prototype system To3D was
   developed by using C++ and OpenGL tools to validate this arithmetic.
   Results indicated that it was effective to reconstruction from isometric
   drawing. And the results also suggest that it is feasible in theory to
   computer aid concept design.},
