   HKSTS; IUE; JSCE; RICS; Urban Planning Soc China; China Civil Engn Soc;
   Hong Kong Inst Util Specialists},
Abstract = {Persistent Scatterer Interferomery (PSI) analysis of land motion in the
   City of Nottingham has been undertaken using ASAR data from the
   ENVISAT-1 satellite covering the period between 2002 and 2009. Some
   interesting features can be seen showing areas of motion in the City. In
   this paper, it is shown that these areas correlate with GPS time series
   levelling data and that they are consistent with geological sources. The
   validation using the various sources of data is also discussed with
   contextual information regarding historical activity. The paper shows
   that land motion in an urban environment can be widespread and
   anisotropic, with many different causes, with the consequences that
   sparse networks of ground-based instruments may be incapable of
   monitoring land motion in such a complex environment.},
