   PEOPLES R CHINA, JUN 15-17, 2009},
Organization = {Int Soc Study Behav Dev; SE Univ, Key Lab Child Dev \& Learning Sci;
   Minist Educ},
Abstract = {This study investigated the associations among the two components of
   ERSBs (Chinese Parental Reactions to Children's Negative Emotions and
   Family Expressiveness), Daily Hassles parents experience, and their
   influences on children's social competence. Both parents of 128 Chinese
   preschoolers rated Emotion-Focused Reactions (EFR) as the behaviors they
   responded with most and Punitive Reactions (PR) least toward children's
   negative emotions. Specifically, mothers behaved with more Distress
   Reactions(DR) and Expressive Encouragement (EE) than fathers did, who
   applied more PR Children's Shyness/Withdrawn Behavior was proved to be
   predicted by more maternal EE and less EFR.. Experienced daily hassles
   with maternal PR and negative expressiveness predicted children's
   aggression. Features of Chinese cultural contexts that influence
   parental emotion-related socialization behaviors and implications are
   discussed.},
