   PEOPLES R CHINA, JUN 15-17, 2009},
Organization = {Int Soc Study Behav Dev; SE Univ, Key Lab Child Dev \& Learning Sci;
   Minist Educ},
Abstract = {Speech emotion recognition, as an important part Of affective computing,
   has giant prospect in applications in a wide variety of fields,
   especially social and emotional development and education field. In this
   paper, a new approach named kernel partial least squares regression is
   introduced for speech emotion recognition. We choose one famous public
   database, namely the Berlin Emotional Speech Database, for experiments
   and extract the global statistic features. The results show that in
   comparison with other current classifiers, kernel partial least squares
   regression improves recognition rates by about 5\% to 22\%.},
