   Minist Educ},
Abstract = {The correlation between infant emotions, including negative emotion and
   positive emotion measured by mother-report and lab observation method
   was investigated in the present study for 69 infants and their mothers
   who were asked to finish the Infant Behavior Questionnaires. The results
   showed for 69 infants that there were no consistencies between the two
   approaches. However, for the girl infants, there were some significant
   correlations in partial subscales between maternal report and laboratory
   observation. It suggested that multimethod should be prudently utilized
   in our future studies.},
