Organization = {Spanish Soc Legal \& Forens Psychol},
Abstract = {Among the different forms of violence against women, one that affects
   most of the population, and perhaps the least known, is sexual
   harrassment. Given the lack of consensus on the definition of this
   problem, is important to define the behaviors and contexts that surround
   them. This study aims to establish whether men and women differ in their
   perception of sexual harrassment depending on the context in which it
   takes place (organizational or interpersonal). It also examines whether
   certain variables that influence ideological perception. The sample
   consists of 69 participants, men and women who answered a questionnaire
   with the measures of interest. Among the main results is that women tend
   to perceive, a greater extent than men, the behaviors described as
   sexual harrassment, and more negative consequences of. these. The
   results of this study could help to increase awareness against sexual
   harrassment, from a better knowledge and definition of this problem, as
   well as to provide guidance to potential victim women of such violence.},
