Abstract = {The character of early sites known from the Indus region is briefly
   discussed. Their relationship to the Indus River and its major
   tributaries is considered, and so also is the large area covered by some
   of the surface sites. An attempt is made to formulate some of the
   problems that confront the prehistorian in understanding the Stone Age
   cultures of the region, especially those of the lower Indus valley which
   is of particular interest because this is where the earliest settlements
