Abstract = {Nature and occurrence of total organic halogen (TOX) in urban river
   waters were surveyed. The features of TOX pollution were characterized
   by its relation with chemical oxygen demand and total nitrogen.  TOX was
   mainly comprised of unpurgable, soluble and stable compounds, but most
   of the TOX components were still unidentified. Considering the results,
   TOX could be a suitable indicator of water quality assessment in terms
   of chemical contamination.},
