Organization = {IUAPPA},
Abstract = {Studies for delineation of air environment strategies were carried out
   for the protection of Taj Mahal and other monuments in the
   Agra-Mathura-Firozabad region. The paper presents the observations on
   air quality status of the region, and estimation of current emissions
   from point area and fine sources. The predictions for air pollution load
   from point sources which are the major contributors have been assessed
   using various air pollution models viz. PTDIS/PTMAX, MPTER, Assimilative
   capacity assessment in Agra city has been evaluated using box model.
   The strategies for protection of Taj Mahal have been projected through
   Air Environment Management Plan which envisages actions at three levels,
   viz. control at the source, control in the source-receptor pathway, and
   at the receptor site. A pragmatic implementation plan for AEMP has also
   been suggested.},
