   Environm Technol SA},
Abstract = {Urban areas affect runoff by increasing its volume and pollutant loads.
   Eventually, urban runoff degrades coastal waters and other receiving
   bodies. An efficient urban runoff management requires that a number of
   objectives are pursued simultaneously alongside with the management
   practice that is applied. In this paper, principal types of pollutants
   found in urban runoff and their potential adverse effects are reviewed.
   Best management measures and practices for urban runoffs are examined.
   As a case study, urban runoff quality measurements in Thessaloniki area,
   conducted recently by the first author, are presented. Moreover, the
   effectiveness of some experimental devices for urban runoff treatment is
   evaluated.},
