Abstract = {A survey was conducted in the province of British Columba, Canada with
   nurse practitioners (NP). This paper reports on the quantitative and
   qualitative findings of the survey questions specifically focused on NP
   perceptions of the clinical impacts associated with using electronic
   medical records (EMRs) in a primary care setting. Findings suggest that
