Pages = {2818-2825},
Note = {International Conference on Energy and Environmental Science (ICEES),
   Singapore, SINGAPORE, OCT, 2011},
Organization = {Singapore Inst Elect (SIE)},
Abstract = {Urban forests have important role on the human habitats including the
   environmental, social and economic aspects. But the accelerated land
   consumption and land abuse are very universal today, the urban forests
   are faced to serious threaten. It is the time to find a new and
   effective theory and method which is used to guide the urban forests
   planning, construction and management. Green Infrastructure (GI) theory
   and practice have roots in planning and conservation efforts that
   started a hundred and fifty years ago in America. Now, it was mature and
   became an important item and method to solving the contradiction between
   urban and rural construction and environment protection in America. GI
   is a network which is composed of ``hubs{''} and ``links{''}, it can
   play an important role at a broad `landscape scale', from urban to
   rural, from site/parcel, regional/local to landscape. In the case study
   presented in this paper, the Cecil County GI planning has contained four
   contents: Cecil County Water Quality Maintenance and Enhancement
   Analysis, Cecil County GI Ecosystem Services Assessment, Cecil County GI
   Network Design and Cecil County GI Implementation Quilt. By the case
   study, it can be seen that GI could be a new method for urban forest
   planning, constructing and managing. (C) 2011 Published by Elsevier Ltd.
   Selection and/or peer-review under responsibility of the Organizers of
   2011 International Conference on Energy and Environmental Science.},
