Organization = {Slovak Acad Sci, Inst Landscape Ecol},
Abstract = {The state of environment and the development of transport network are
   related with the impact that transport network exerts on the habitat,
   migration routes and reproduction conditions for wildlife. Such impact
   has spatial character, and eventually results in the extinction of
   certain species or communities and fragmentation of biogeocoenotic
   cover. Preliminary general assessment of the effect of fragmentation and
   a pilot region case are presented. The produced map, which reflects the
   impact of the highways and settlement network (including urban areas) on
   biocoenoses in Ukraine, was used for correction of planning the
   eco-corridors.},
