   International-Society-for-the-Study-of-Behavioural-Development, nanjing,
   PEOPLES R CHINA, JUN 15-17, 2009},
Organization = {Int Soc Study Behav Dev; SE Univ, Key Lab Child Dev \& Learning Sci;
   Minist Educ},
Abstract = {Fear emotion video was presented as emotional stimulus to children with
   autism and healthy children as control to explore the relationship
   between impairment of emotion processing in autism and disruption of
   prefrontal area in a functional near infrared spectroscopy (NIRS) study.
   Compared with healthy control group, the response of oxy-hemoglobin
   (oxy-Hb) in prefrontal cortex, especially in ventromedial prefrontal
   cortex, was lower for children with autism. It was indicated that
   emotional cognition of autism is inferior to healthy children; the level
   of activation of prefrontal is different between two groups. This result
   suggested the mode of emotional processing in autism is novel compared
   to healthy children. There was no significant difference in emotion
   intensity for two groups.},
