   European-Academy-for-Sustainable-Development (EURACA), Athens, GREECE,
   SEP 04-06, 2019},
Organization = {European Acad Sustainable Dev; Technologies \& Mat Renewable Energy
   Environm \& Sustainabil},
Abstract = {In this work the issues of efficient isolated stand-alone PV systems
   that at the same time perform the functions of hardscape (fountains and
   small architectural forms) or sculptures items have been discussed. The
   solutions based on flat-type PV modules and CPV modules based toroidal
   concentrators for traditional sculptures, organic sculptures, as well as
   those in urban style have been presented. One other objective of
   research was to get this approach noticed and to show that solar
   installations can be blend naturally with historical parks and palace
   complexes (on the example of Peterhof), museums without disturbing their
   esthetics built over a period of centuries. The purpose of this work is
   to prove the possibility, effectiveness and expedience of solar
   installations having forms designed to match different environments
   without breaking the harmony of the surrounding nature and landscape.
   One other objective of research was to get this approach noticed and to
   show that solar PV systems can be blend naturally into historical series
   of parks and gardens, museums without disturbing their esthetics built
   over a period of centuries},
