   Psychiat Assoc; Aristotle Univ Thessaloniki, Sch Med},
Abstract = {The purpose is to study ``exodus{''} of emotion in the face. In a sample
   of 144 children (6, 9 and 11 years old, 24 boys and 24 girls in each
   team), their effort to express the emotion which was provoked by
   listening to music arousing them emotionally and admission of a
   repulsive intellectual picture during listening was video-recorded,
   registering what the child felt on average during listening. Four judges
   watched the video-cassette without sound and marked the expressed
   emotion on a 7-grade scale. Negative thoughts are certainly able to
   block the evolution of already started (mainly positive) emotions as an
   experience and as an expression, mostly in 9 years old children (mainly,
   girls: sadness, boys: happiness), but neurophysical, in 6 years old
   children, and psychosocial, in 11 years old children, reasons reduce
   expressing of emotions.},
