   Antalya, TURKEY, MAY 25-29, 2011},
Abstract = {Service industry gained importance in recent periods. Call Centers have
   been situated within that sector in which emotions are most intensively
   used. For competitiveness, understanding the emotional processes is
   important. Therefore, the aim of this study is to understand the effect
   emotional dissonance has on turnover intentions and absenteeism, and the
   moderating effect of quality of work life perceptions for call center
   employees. The study was conducted with 318 Turkish call center
   employees. A significant positive effect was found regarding emotional
   dissonance on turnover intentions and on unexcused absenteeism. Instead
   of functioning as a moderator, quality of work life perceptions affected
   turnover intentions and absenteeism directly.},
