   Politehnica Univ Timisoara, Timisoara, ROMANIA, OCT 17-18, 2019},
Organization = {IEEE Power \& Energy Soc; World Energy Council, Comitetul Natl Roman;
   Honeywell; Elster; Continental; Engie; Opt SWD},
Abstract = {Urban pollution is now the biggest worldwide environmental risk to
   health. To improve air quality the existing solutions cannot be easily
   implemented in existing dense urban districts. The Urban Wet
   ElectroStatic Precipitator project is dedicated to the design and
   evaluation of a new urban air cleanup system based on two-stage wet
   electrostatic precipitation units. Each unit, which looks like a small
   footprint vertical rainwater downpipe, can be fixed on the external
   facade of buildings and thus can be deployable in such districts.
   Moreover those units can collect particles of a diameter down to 0.1 mu
   m and absorb gaseous compounds (as NOx or SO2) while consuming little
   energy. In each unit, ionized polluted air flows downward in annular
   collecting chambers limited up and down by two helical ramps. This air
   gradually yields its particles and gaseous compounds to a co-current
   film flow which is released into sewers at the foot of buildings.},
